                <pb facs="0445" n="363" xml:id="pg363"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/421.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Mexican Ambassador.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Memorandum.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1910-11-16"><hi rendition="#italic">November 16,
                        1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The Department of State is in receipt of two memoranda of the Embassy of Mexico,
                    both of to-day’s date, stating [etc.].</p>
                <p>The Department of State hastens to inform the ambassador of Mexico that the
                    contents of the above memoranda have already been communicated to the Department
                    of Justice with the recommendations for immediate action required by the urgency
                    of the case.</p>
            </div>
